alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "The style_oracle entry, invoked as `style_oracle MODE REPS PAGE UA [SUFFIX=SHEET ...]` with every path relative to the working directory, as tests/css/style_oracle.mjs and research/investigations/style/run.sh run it. PAGE is parsed by pkg::html::tree_builder::parse_document with scripting off, as the reference browser runs without script. UA is added with pkg::style::add_sheet as the user-agent sheet; then the page's sheets are added in tree order as pkg::style::sheet_sources lists them: a style element with add_style_element, and a stylesheet link whose href ends with the SUFFIX of some argument, the longest such suffix, by reading that argument's SHEET as an author sheet when the link has no media attribute or one that pkg::style::media_holds; a link no argument maps is skipped. The style attributes are added last. The environment is a 1280 by 720 viewport with a 16px root font size, and the default fonts the reference browser draws on its Linux host through fontconfig: Liberation Serif for serif (x-height 940 and zero advance 1024 of 2048 units, from its OS/2 table and hmtx), Liberation Sans for sans-serif (1082 and 1139) and DejaVu Sans Mono for monospace (1233 for the zero; it has no OS/2 x-height, so the x glyph's height of 1120 units, rounded up to whole pixels as the browser measures it). MODE dump computes the styles once and writes to standard output the file format of tests/css/style_oracle.mjs: a header line, then one line per element in preorder with its index, its local name and the computed value of each of the 55 longhands of pkg::css::values in their order, serialized as Chromium's computedStyleMap serializes them. MODE match, inherited, reset or all runs the stage REPS times up to and including that part and writes one line `MODE elements N rules R`, followed for all by the number of distinct values of each group; REPS 0 runs only the parsing and sheet loading, so a timing difference isolates the parts. MODE structure takes SCRIPT in place of REPS: S lines add author sheets before any edit, B PARENT BEFORE TEXT inserts a paragraph (BEFORE is a NodeId or - to append; backslash-n and doubled backslashes in TEXT are unescaped as in the layout oracle), and X NODE detaches a subtree. Each edit independently matches the whole document before and after, pairs surviving elements by NodeId, and compares winning declarations, custom-rule keys and pseudo-elements against structural_restyle of the changed parent. It prints `structure I set S changed C missing M` (plus ` first NODE` on a miss), or `structure I full changed C`, and exits with 1 if any edit misses an element. It exits with 0 on success and with 2 and a message on standard error for a usage error, an unreadable file or a refusal of the stage.";
